  "notes": "Voice-engine test video (D13 trial): one actor, five impressions, each with its own Chatterbox reference (real game voice clips in clips/ref-*.wav, built by make_refs.py in projects/casting-call) and its own look. Director = Kokoro bm_fable so the host never sounds like an impression. Standard shape kept: bare opening with the title + one line (and one transform), screen broken with the mic, black, then the CTA — here spoken by the five forms, one piece each. Alternative hooks: 'One actor. Five voices.' / 'Casting call. Bring everyone.' / 'He does voices. All of them.' v4: stand mic (never behind the head), director permanently bored (typing/arms crossed, no reaction), Jinx words at emotion 0.95 + separate laugh beat, SpongeBob catchphrases + snail line, mic thrown off the stand into the screen (mic_stuck), ending on a clean screen, ASR read-back retakes for unclear lines. v6: opening = the whole panel (five forms seated in a circle with a water table, actor centre in the spotlight, no early transform); director drawn and voiced as J. Jonah Jameson (ref-jjj.wav); stand mic fixed in space at chest height; Vegeta armour with navy outlines.",
